! EVE$HELP.HLP: help for EVE's commands and keys. vaxpunk's own text.
! A command of several words is a topic of its first word, with a
! subtopic for each word after it, so HELP ERASE START OF LINE finds it.
1 DO
  Press Do to give EVE a command. EVE asks "Command:" at the bottom of
  the screen; type the command and press Return.

  Each word of a command can be cut short, as long as what you type
  starts only one command: MO D is MOVE DOWN. Whatever follows the
  command's words is its parameter, as in FIND hello or LINE 20. A
  command that needs a parameter you didn't give asks for it.

  HELP KEYS shows what the keys do.
1 KEYS
  The editing keypad, above the arrows:

    +---------+---------+---------+
    |  Find   | Insert  | Remove  |     Do      a command
    |         |  Here   |         |     Help    help
    +---------+---------+---------+     F10     EXIT
    | Select  |  Prev   |  Next   |     F12     START OF LINE
    |         | Screen  | Screen  |     F13     ERASE PREVIOUS WORD
    +---------+---------+---------+     F14     CHANGE MODE

  The arrow keys are MOVE UP, MOVE DOWN, MOVE LEFT and MOVE RIGHT.
  Return breaks the line, Tab puts in a tab and Delete is DELETE.

    Ctrl/A   CHANGE MODE            Ctrl/R   REMEMBER
    Ctrl/E   END OF LINE            Ctrl/U   ERASE START OF LINE
    Ctrl/H   START OF LINE (BS)     Ctrl/V   QUOTE
    Ctrl/J   ERASE WORD (LF)        Ctrl/W   REFRESH
    Ctrl/L   INSERT PAGE BREAK      Ctrl/Z   EXIT

  DEFINE KEY and LEARN put commands on keys of your own.
1 BOTTOM
  Moves the cursor to the end of the buffer.
1 BUFFER
  Makes a buffer the one in the window: BUFFER name. EVE makes the
  buffer, empty, if there is none of that name.
1 CAPITALIZE
2 WORD
  Makes the first letter of the word at the cursor a capital and the
  rest small letters, then moves past the word.
1 CENTER
2 LINE
  Puts the text of the current line half way between the left and right
  margins. The cursor goes to the start of the text.
1 CHANGE
2 DIRECTION
  Turns the buffer's direction around, forward to reverse or reverse to
  forward. The status line shows the direction.
2 MODE
  Switches the buffer between insert and overstrike mode. The status
  line shows the mode. Ctrl/A and F14 do it too.
1 DEFINE
2 KEY
  Puts a command on a key: DEFINE KEY command. EVE asks you to press the
  key; from then on the key does the command.
1 DELETE
  Deletes the character before the cursor. At the start of a line, the
  line joins the one before it. The Delete key does it.
2 BUFFER
  Deletes a buffer: DELETE BUFFER name, the current buffer if you give
  no name. EVE asks first if the buffer was changed and not written.
  The only buffer can't be deleted.
1 END
2 OF
3 LINE
  Moves the cursor to the end of the line. Ctrl/E does it too.
1 ERASE
2 CHARACTER
  Erases the character at the cursor. RESTORE CHARACTER puts it back.
2 LINE
  Erases the current line, its line end too. RESTORE LINE or RESTORE
  puts it back.
2 PREVIOUS
3 WORD
  Erases the word before the cursor; at the start of a word, the one
  before it. At the start of a line it joins the line to the one
  before. RESTORE WORD puts the word back. F13 does it.
2 START
3 OF
4 LINE
  Erases from the start of the line up to the cursor. Ctrl/U does it.
2 WORD
  Erases the word at the cursor and the spaces after it. At the end of
  a line, the next line joins this one after a space. RESTORE WORD puts
  the word back. Ctrl/J does it.
1 EXIT
  Ends the session, writing each buffer you changed to its file. F10
  and Ctrl/Z do it too.
1 FILL
2 PARAGRAPH
  Fills the paragraph the cursor is in, the lines between blank lines,
  so that its words fit between the left and right margins.
1 FIND
  Finds text: FIND text. EVE looks from the cursor in the buffer's
  direction, and puts the cursor on what it finds. Text in small letters
  finds either case; with a capital in it, only that case. If the text
  is only the other way, EVE asks whether to go there.

  The Find key asks for the text.
2 NEXT
  Finds the text the last FIND looked for, again.
1 FORWARD
  Makes the buffer's direction forward, toward its end.
1 GET
2 FILE
  Edits a file: GET FILE name. The file goes in a buffer of its own,
  which the window then shows; if a buffer has the file already, EVE
  shows that one.
1 GLOBAL
2 REPLACE
  Replaces text everywhere in the buffer without asking: GLOBAL REPLACE
  old. EVE asks for the new text, and tells how many it replaced. The
  cursor stays where it was.
1 GO
2 TO
  Moves the cursor to a mark that MARK made: GO TO name.
1 HELP
  Shows help on a command or topic: HELP topic. The Help key shows help
  too. HELP KEYS shows the keys, HELP DO how to give commands.
1 INCLUDE
2 FILE
  Puts a file's text in the buffer at the cursor: INCLUDE FILE name.
1 INSERT
2 HERE
  Puts the text that REMOVE or STORE TEXT saved in at the cursor. The
  Insert Here key does it.
2 MODE
  Makes typing put characters in, pushing the rest of the line right.
2 PAGE
3 BREAK
  Puts a form feed, a page break, on a line of its own at the cursor.
  Ctrl/L does it.
1 LEARN
  Starts learning keys: what you press next, up to Ctrl/R, EVE then
  puts on a key of your choice. See REMEMBER.
1 LINE
  Moves the cursor to the start of a line by its number: LINE n.
1 LOWERCASE
2 WORD
  Makes the word at the cursor small letters, then moves past it.
1 MARK
  Marks the cursor's place with a name: MARK name. GO TO name comes back
  to it.
1 MOVE
2 BY
3 LINE
  Moves to the end of the line, or of the next one if the cursor is
  there already, when the direction is forward; to the start of the
  line, or of the one before, when it is reverse.
3 WORD
  Moves to the next word when the direction is forward, the one before
  when it is reverse.
2 DOWN
  Moves the cursor down a line. The down arrow does it.
2 LEFT
  Moves the cursor left a character. The left arrow does it.
2 RIGHT
  Moves the cursor right a character, past the end of the line too. The
  right arrow does it.
2 UP
  Moves the cursor up a line. The up arrow does it.
1 NEXT
2 BUFFER
  Shows the next buffer in the window.
2 SCREEN
  Moves a screen on, toward the end of the buffer. The Next Screen key
  does it.
2 WINDOW
  With two windows, moves the cursor to the other one.
1 ONE
2 WINDOW
  Goes back to one window, showing the current buffer.
1 OTHER
2 WINDOW
  With two windows, moves the cursor to the other one.
1 OVERSTRIKE
2 MODE
  Makes typing replace the characters at the cursor.
1 PREVIOUS
2 BUFFER
  Shows the buffer before the current one in the window.
2 SCREEN
  Moves a screen back, toward the start of the buffer. The Prev Screen
  key does it.
2 WINDOW
  With two windows, moves the cursor to the other one.
1 QUIT
  Ends the session without writing the buffers. If you changed one, EVE
  asks first.
1 QUOTE
  Puts the next character you type in the buffer as it is, a control
  character too. Ctrl/V does it.
1 REFRESH
  Draws the screen again. Ctrl/W does it.
1 REMEMBER
  Ends LEARN: EVE asks you to press a key, which from then on does the
  keys learned. Ctrl/R does it.
1 REMOVE
  Moves the text selected, or found, into the insert-here buffer. INSERT
  HERE puts it back somewhere else. The Remove key does it.
1 REPEAT
  Does a key more than once: REPEAT n. EVE asks you to press the key,
  and does what it does n times.
1 REPLACE
  Replaces text, asking each time: REPLACE old. EVE asks for the new
  text, then at each place from the cursor on asks Yes, No, All (the
  rest without asking), Last (this one, then stop) or Quit.
1 RESET
  Cancels the selection.
1 RESTORE
  Puts back the line ERASE LINE erased, as RESTORE LINE does.
2 CHARACTER
  Puts back the characters ERASE CHARACTER or ERASE START OF LINE
  erased last.
2 LINE
  Puts back the line ERASE LINE erased last, above the current line.
2 WORD
  Puts back the word ERASE WORD or ERASE PREVIOUS WORD erased last.
1 REVERSE
  Makes the buffer's direction reverse, toward its start.
1 SAVE
2 FILE
  Writes the current buffer to its file.
3 AS
  Writes the current buffer to another file, SAVE FILE AS name, which
  becomes the buffer's file.
1 SELECT
  Starts a selection at the cursor. Move the cursor, and the text in
  between is selected, for REMOVE or STORE TEXT. The Select key does it.
2 ALL
  Selects the whole buffer.
1 SET
2 LEFT
3 MARGIN
  Sets the buffer's left margin, a column: SET LEFT MARGIN n.
2 RIGHT
3 MARGIN
  Sets the buffer's right margin, a column: SET RIGHT MARGIN n.
2 TABS
  Puts tab stops every n columns: SET TABS n.
1 SHOW
2 BUFFERS
  Lists the buffers, with their lines and files, in a buffer of its own.
1 START
2 OF
3 LINE
  Moves the cursor to the start of the line. F12 and Backspace do it.
1 STORE
2 TEXT
  Copies the text selected, or found, into the insert-here buffer,
  leaving it where it is. INSERT HERE puts a copy in elsewhere.
1 TOP
  Moves the cursor to the start of the buffer.
1 TPU
  Does a TPU statement: TPU statement, such as TPU POSITION (END_OF
  (CURRENT_BUFFER)).
1 TWO
2 WINDOWS
  Splits the screen into two windows, both showing the current buffer.
1 UPPERCASE
2 WORD
  Makes the word at the cursor capitals, then moves past it.
1 WRITE
2 FILE
  Writes the current buffer: WRITE FILE name, to its own file if you
  give no name.
